Guidelines for the FastJet Contrib area
---------------------------------------

The FastJet contrib area is intended for developers of FastJet-related
tools to provide easy access to their work in a common, publicly
accessible location.

If you wish to add code to the fastjet-contrib repository, please
follow the guidelines indicated below.

For further information about making contributions, please contact
fastjet@projects.hepforge.org

======================================================================
Basic Requirements
==================

Each contribution must be in a directory of its own, ideally a
subdirectory of plugins/ or tools/.

Each contribution is the responsibility of its authors. The FastJet
authors will not provide support. 

Each contribution should be made available under the terms of the GNU
General Public License (v2 or later), or if the author wishes, under a
more permissive license.

Each contribution should include the following files:

 - COPYING: giving license information

 - AUTHORS: names of authors, including current email addresses

 - README: giving a basic explanation of the scope and usage of the
   contrib and indication of which work should be cited by users of
   your code. Please mention any external dependencies, e.g. ROOT,
   GSL, Boost, etc. 

 - an example program using the contrib tool or plugin, together with
   a file containing the expected output.

We also strongly encourage the presence of the following files:

 - ChangeLog: with explanations of the main changes and when they were made
 - VERSION: a version number, e.g. 1.0.x, which would be updated to
   2.0.x in the event of a major change.

======================================================================
Build system
============

Each contribution should also include a Makefile. 

 - The Makefile should prominently define a variable FASTJETCONFIG
   near the beginning of the file. By default FASTJETCONFIG should be
   set to fastjet-config, i.e. the contribution should build out of
   the box if fastjet-config is in the user's path.

 - The Makefile should include the targets "all" and "clean"; make all
   should also build the example. There is no convention for "install"
   at this stage.

======================================================================
General remarks
===============

Never commit an incomplete version or one that does not compile. If
you need to have a working area for development, use a branch. If your
contrib normally lives in trunk/plugins/XXX/, the branch should be
branches/plugins-XXX-info-about-branch/

The maintainers of the FastJet Contrib area reserve the right to
reorganise the directory structure if it appears to be
appropriate. They may occasionally fix minor bugs, but will generally
aim to consult with the authors in such cases. Contributors should not
commit modifications to parts of the contrib that are not theirs,
without first consulting the relevant authors.





